      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "The ratio of the width of a volleyball court to its length is $\\frac{1}{2}.$ If the length of the volleyball court is $18$ meters, what is its width?",
      "worked_solution": "The ratio of width to length is $\\frac{1}{2}.$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the width and the denominator represents the length.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $18$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $9$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1\\times 9}{2\\times 9}=\\frac{9}{18}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the width of the volleyball court is $9$ meters.",
